rmatics tools  in order to identify the mutanome or  mutations present within cancerous  tissue  that are not expressed in wild-type  cells  the metanome will then be put through  bioinformatics algorithms  to identify the predictive  immunogenicity and pcv efficacy of each  individual neoantigen  the top neoantogen peptide candidates  will be synthetically produced and used  for in-vitro functionality screening  in order to confirm the predicted  activity of each candidate  from these results clinicians will first  decide on the 20 or so neo antigens  which they plan to use for their  patients pcb  and secondly decide which modality they  will use  to introduce those neo antigens to the  patient's lymphatic system  the most common modalities include  neo-antigen dna  mrna peptide or post antigen presenting  cells mixed with varying delivery  vehicles and adjuvants  once formalized the vaccine will be  placed directly into the patient's  lymphatic system  through injection in order to be  processed and presented by patient apcs  and initiate a t-cell-based  anti-tumor-killing immune response  against cancerous tissue expressing  those neoantigen epitopes  the second main therapeutic targeting  neoantogens are personalized t cell  therapies  the main difference between personalized  t-cell therapies and off-the-shelf  treatments i described earlier  is that they are tailored to immunogenic  neoantigen on patient-specific tumors  similar to pcvs the first stage of  personalized t-cell development  is to biopsy and sequence the patient's  tumor to identify the mutanum  which is put through bioinformatics  algorithms to identify neoantigens  are predicted to initiate a strong  immune cascade when they bind to tcrs  these neoantigen candidates will be  synthetically produced  and screened for therapeutic efficacy in  order to identify the perfect neoantogen  for an individual's tumor  from there a tcr will be engineered to  express binding domains  for that specific neoantogen and cloned  into patient-specific  known as autologous or healthy donor  known as allergenic t  cells those t cells are expanded and  infused into the patient  in order to elicit an anti-tumor-killing  immune response  no matter the type of neoantigen  targeted therapeutic researchers will  require production of synthetic  neoantigen peptides during three phases  first neoantogen peptides are required  for preclinical functionality screening  of bioinformatics candidates  for t cell therapy these peptides will  be utilized for tcr binding affinity and  immunogenicity analysis  while neoantogen candidates for pcv  development will be used for t cell  stimulation assays such as ellie spots  flow cytometry and cytotoxicity assays  after a new therapeutic has been  developed it will be  first tested in animals such as mice and  non-human primates  not just for efficacy testing but mainly  for safety and toxicity of  novel additions to the therapeutic such  as adjuvants and delivery vehicles like  lipo or nanoparticles  for this stage of development of pcvs  neoantigen peptides will be used as  model vaccines to inject into the  animals  as well as for post-clinical efficacy  screening  during this phase whether it be in  animals or human patients  neoantogen peptides are utilized to  ensure that the intervention  initiated an immune response which can  be continuously used to target and kill  neoantogen expressing cancerous tissue  despite neoantigen peptides being  required for multiple stages of  personalized therapeutic development  they tend to be the bottleneck for many  researchers trying to produce these  treatments in a timely manner  due to the difficulty of neoantogen  peptide synthesis  but how do we synthesize peptides  let's review the basics of synthetic  peptide synthesis  peptides can be produced using either  recombinant or synthetic technologies  recombinant synthesis is simply  expressing the peptide within a  microorganism  through standard plasma transfection and  peptide purification  chemical synthesis on the other hand is  much more involved but basically a resin  is used to anchor the first amino acid  in the peptide chain  while additional amino acids are added  one by one through a standard  dehydration reaction between the amino  and carboxyl groups of the supporting  and incoming amino acid these two  synthetic methodologies can also be  combined  depending on the specific amino acid  sequence which needs to be produced  at genscript we prefer to use synthetic  peptide production  because it's easier to custom design any  peptide sequence  produce longer peptides through ligation  of shorter fragments  and to generate large-scale peptides  while recombinant expression has  limitations  for incorporating unnatural amino acids  or modifications  it's difficult to synthesize hydrophobic  peptides  an overexpression of membrane peptides  can actually harm the cell and lead to  cell death  let's dive a little deeper into chemical  peptide production  chemical peptide synthesis most often  occurs by coupling the carboxyl group  of the incoming amino acid to the  n-terminus of the growing peptide chain  this c to n synthesis is opposite from  protein biosynthesis  in order to accomplish this each amino  acid will go through protection of  reactive groups  this ensures that when new amino acids  are added to the growing chain  they bind in the c to n format rather  than through the side chain  once protected the first amino acid will  be linked to a resin through its c  terminal so that new amino acids can be  coupled to that amino acids and terminal  as shown here in step three once the  growing amino acid chain is finished  all of the protective groups will be  removed in order to have a fully  reactive peptide this peptide will then  be purified from the resin  using high performance liquid  chromatography or hplc  as you can see through this example  chromatogram in step 5.  at denscript we use three different  types of chemical synthesis  liquid phase synthesis is the original  methodology for synthetic peptide  production  and unlike solid-based synthesis does  not require linking of the first amino  acid to a resin  but instead requires an additional  chemical protective group  on the c-terminus of the first amino  acid because of this synthetic  technology  each new peptide must be manually  purified before addition of the next  amino acid  now while this can be timely and costly  it also ensures  extremely high purity of the final  peptide  also because the c-terminus is not  attached to a resin  it is the preferred method for any  peptide requiring c-terminal  modifications  and is great for large yields solid  phase synthesis is similar to liquid  phase synthesis  however instead of a protective group on  the first amino acid  the c-terminal is linked to a resin this  makes addition of new amino acids  easy and smooth and therefore  significantly reduces turnaround time  as purification can wait until the end  because of the technology  solid phase synthesis is preferred for  long and difficult peptides rather than  bulk production  the most recent advancement in peptide  synthesis is through the use of  automated microwave technology rather  than manual synthesis  microwave synthesis is done entirely  through a machine  and therefore it can significantly  reduce the turnaround time and increase  the overall capacity  to make larger numbers of peptides per  day  in fact genscript's microwave technology  actually doubled our capacity  so now we can chemically synthesize 18  000 peptides per month  because this technology uses microwave  energy it is able to increase turnaround  time by reducing the time required for  coupling and resin separation  this also makes it great for fast  synthesis of difficult shorter peptides  rather than longer ones  the reason we utilize three different  types of chemical synthesis  and a combination thereof including  recombinant production  is because each peptide's intrinsic  characteristics will dictate if a  peptide is difficult to synthesize  and why neo-antigen peptides tend to be  highly difficult to produce  and will require all different types of  synthesis in order to produce highly  pure peptides at required yields  specifically neo-antigen peptides can be  difficult to synthesize  because of these five characteristics  listed here  peptide length charge hydrophobicity  yield and purity for length neoantigen  tend to either be 9 to 11 amino acids  representing the  neoantigen epitope or they will be  larger than 25 amino acids in order to  be processed and presented  by apc's on mhc class 1 and class 2.  peptides over 20 amino acids tend to be  difficult to synthesize and will usually  require a combination of microwave and  solid-based synthesis  for peptide charge because neoantogens  are only expressed in cancer  they tend to contain charge-modifying  amino acids which would not be expressed  within natural  tumor-associated antigens many synthetic  steps  only work with specific isoelectric  points and therefore the further from  neutral a peptide is  the synthesis will be more difficult  third  because neo antigens are produced from  random amino acid indels throughout the  peptide  hydrophobic side chains are bound to be  introduced within the sequence  these hydrophobic side chains will lead  to a stronger chance of aggregation  and therefore limited solubility in  water which in turn makes purification  very difficult neoantogen peptide  synthesis can also be very difficult  because each application within the  various stages of therapeutic  development  will require completely different yields  or peptide mass  as well as purity or percentage of  target peptide within a sample  because of the flexibility required it  can be cumbersome to find a reliable  provider  which is able to accommodate yields  ranging from large-scale micro libraries  of  half a milligram to synthesis of gram  level of one individual peptide  because of this genscript has tailored  its neoantigen peptide synthesis service  to be fully customizable in order to  achieve yields for any application  in terms of purity other than  flexibility required for various  applications  because neolinogen peptides tend to be  hydrophobic and have a tendency to  aggregate  their solubility makes them difficult to  purify using standard techniques  because of this they must be treated  with extra care and go through  additional processes of purification  in order to reach the 98 purity required  for applications like personalized  cancer vaccine generation  and analysis in patient-derived cell  lines  as these are precious samples  in order to accomplish difficult  neo-antigen peptide synthesis  we here at genscript have developed our  own neoantigen peptide synthesis  platform  which utilizes reliable technologies and  tools to achieve a 95  success rate for difficult peptide  synthesis this platform can be divided  into four main stages  in the first stage every neoantigen  peptide sequence which comes through our  order system  is analyzed by our proprietary natal  pre-bioinformatics algorithm  in order to determine synthetic  difficulty and the best method to  synthesize  each peptide based on its predicted  difficulty  in the second stage of genscript's  platform those neoantogen peptides will  be synthesized according to the  recommendation of our neopre algorithm  and our peptide experts using one or a  combination of our synthetic  technologies  ranging from manual liquid and or solid  phase automated microwave technology  recombinant expression or chemical  ligation  in order to understand how we achieve  this 95  success rate for highly difficult  peptides let's dive a little deeper into  gemscript's neopre  analytics tool  genscript's long-standing experience in  peptide synthesis has given us an  opportunity to develop a tool for  estimating ease of peptide synthesis  process  it is necessary to evaluate the  feasibility of all peptide sequences  prior to synthesis  therefore every one of our customers  peptides go through our proprietary  neopre bioinformatics algorithm  to determine synthesis difficulty the  first step in using this tool  is to copy the neoantogen peptide  sequence into the algorithm shown here  if this is the customer facing tool then  once you hit submit you will see a  response indicating how difficult the  synthesis of the peptide will be  if this tool is being used internally  the readout will be much more involved  and highlight the individual  characteristics  that are causing difficult synthesis as  well as the recombinant  or sorry recommended synthetic synthetic  technology  this slide shows an example of what the  readout of the internal algorithm would  look like  the algorithm would analyze the  individual peptide sequences and convert  its intrinsic characteristics to numbers  which correspond to how difficult the  peptide synthesis will be  due to that specific characteristics the  six characteristics that neoprene  analyzes  our tendency for the peptide to  aggregate represented by na4vss  isoelectric point shown as pi  hydrophobicity  sequence length yield and purity  amino acids are shown in red during the  system review  to indicate which ones have strong  tendency to aggregate  for aggregation less than 0 is  considered simple  0 to 20 is considered middle and over 20  is considered hard  while larger hydrophobicity numbers  indicate more difficult sequences  once the algorithm has assessed each  peptide's difficulty  it will determine the predicted  difficulty of synthesizing each peptide  as well as recommend the best means of  successfully synthesizing each  individual peptide  once the just peptide expert reviews the  results they will then adjust the  synthetic methodology as needed based  off javascript 15 years of peptide  synthesis  neopre is able to analyze the numerical  values assigned to individual  characteristics of each peptide in order  to predict the synthetic difficulty  overall genscript has used neopre for  171 peptides for this specific case  study  of those 71 were shown to be difficult  to synthesize  of the 71 difficult peptides 61 were  actually difficult to synthesize  while 10 were actually easier to  synthesize than originally predicted  digging deeper a hundred peptides were  shown to be easy to synthesize  with 78 of them accurately predicted and  22 of them  actually difficult to synthesize with  this tool what's important to understand  is that those 83 total difficult  peptides  were able to be synthesized despite  their high hydrophobicity  long length and tendency to aggregate  since using neopre genscript has  actually been able to synthesize  2158 out of 2267 peptides ordered  giving us an overall success rate of  95.15 percent  37.5 percent of which were delivered  using genscript's rush peptide service  within  five to six days neoantogen peptides  tend to either be focused on epitopes  presented on mhc1 and mhc2 which range  from 9 to 15 amino acids  or they tend to be larger over 20 amino  acids  for 9 to 15 amino acids genscript  synthesized 1835  out of 1806 peptides ordered  giving an overall success rate of 98.18  percent  with the majority of these peptides  being deemed as difficult  synthesizing the larger peptides over 20  amino acids  always tend to be more difficult and  require more attention in synthetic  methodology  and take slightly longer because of this  genscript has synthesized 85.31  of ordered larger peptides  after each neoantogen peptide has been  synthesized  using our neopre and synthetic  technologies they will go through  stringent quality control based  on individual customer and application  needs  all genscript peptides undergo total  quality management testing  including mass spectrometry and  analytical hplc  high performance liquid chromatography  analysis throughout the peptide  synthesis and purification process  through our trademarked acupep quality  control service in addition to the  standard coa document you would receive  genscript offers an additional 12  quality control services  including our endotoxin analysis and  removal service  endotoxins are lipopolysaccharides which  are major components of the cell walls  of gram-negative bacteria  which can be introduced into custom  peptide preparations during synthesis  more importantly they can stimulate a  plethora of unwanted immune reactions in  b cells  macrophages as well as stimulate t cell  expansion even at the lowest  concentration  to enhance your experimental results  genscript offers custom peptides with  guaranteed endotoxin control service  to reduce endotoxin levels at less than  0.01 eu per microgram  which is ideal for most cellular assays  especially on primary cell lines  we also offer guaranteed tfa  measurements and removal  tfa or trifluoroacetic acid is a strong  acid which is commonly used to cleave  synthesized peptides from solid-based  resins  and is also used to improve hplc  performance in the peptide purification  step  although tfa is quite important residual  tfa and custom peptides can cause  inexplicable discrepancies  in subsequent assay data which is why at  gen script we can guarantee tfa values  of less than one percent  in exchange for either acetate or  formate  the last step of junscript's neoantigen  peptide synthesis platform  is peptide optimization in which we can  design seven different types of peptide  libraries in order to narrow down your  perfect neoantigen sequence  the most popular peptide library design  services for neoantogen peptides  are genscript's alanine scanning  overlapping and t cell truncation  libraries  in an alanine scanning library each  amino acid will  sequentially be replaced with an alanine  in turn  this will allow the end user to  determine the most important individual  amino acids to peptide function  as opposed to an alanine scanning  library which replaces individual amino  acids  an overlapping library simply deletes  amino acids over a certain threshold  because of this it is great for  identifying where a neoantogen epitope  is within an  entire neoantigen peptide sequence t  cell truncation libraries are similar to  overlapping libraries  except you can decide on multiple  epitope lengths to put into one pool  in order to tease out the perfect length  of your neoantigen or tcr  i know i have gone over a lot of  information about neo-antigen peptides  and how they are used in personalized  cancer medicine  so now i would like to summarize the key  takeaways from today's presentation  first neoantogens are new or novel  cancer antigens which are present on  cancerous tissue  but not expressed within wild-type  tissue they are expressed within  individual tumors  or tumor cells of a specific patient  rather than being shared amongst  patients suffering from one type of  cancer  second normally neoantogens are not  expressed at a high enough level to be  tracked by the immune system  but because they are not recognized as  self antigens  like common tumor-associated antigens  they are highly immunogenic  third neo-antigen therapeutics can be  either personalized cancer vaccines or  personalized t-cell therapies  both of these therapeutics require  neo-antigen peptides for various stages  of functionality and efficacy screening  fourth genscript's neopre bioinformatics  algorithm  allows javascript to synthesize highly  hydrophobic difficult peptides  by analyzing the individual amino acid  sequence  for hydrophobicity length aggregation  charge yield and purity to identify  synthetic difficulty  and the technology to synthesize each  peptide  and lastly genscript's neoantigen  peptide services  offer a reliable synthesis by being a  trustworthy partner  having a high success rate for difficult  peptide synthesis  and flexible services for all precision  therapeutic applications  i want to thank you for attending my  presentation today and i am happy to  answer any questions you may have  but while you are typing your questions  into the chat box i would quickly like  to mention  that genscript's neoantigen peptide  synthesis service produces reliable  neoantigen peptides for precision  therapeutic discovery  this is because at gen script we have  the technical means and experience to  synthesize large numbers of challenging  neoantogen peptides  and provide tailored optimization tools  for your downstream applications  we are able to accomplish this by  providing a trustworthy user experience  demonstrated through our work with over  50 of the world's leading immuno  oncology organizations  at 95 success rate for difficult  neoantogen peptide synthesis  and our extreme service flexibility  putting our customers in the driver's  seat of their entire project  no matter what the application again  thank you for your attention and i am  looking forward to answering your  questions  thank you
 

